  "step_2": "The individual considers the risk involved in pursuing an extra 100 Euros (i.e., the difference between 2500 and 2400 Euros). The verbal report 'Das Risiko für die extra 100€ lohnt nicht' translates to 'The risk for the extra 100€ is not worth it.' This indicates that the individual weighed the potential gain of 100 Euros (from 2400 to 2500) against the risk of getting nothing (0 Euros with 1% probability) and the certainty of losing the potential gain (since there is a 66% chance of getting only 2400 Euros instead of 2500). The individual justifies the choice by rejecting the risk associated with the extra 100 Euros, implying a preference for the certain 2400 Euros over the uncertain higher amount.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the probability of achieving the maximum outcome: it prefers the lottery with the higher probability of the highest possible payoff. In this case, Lottery B has a 100% chance of the maximum outcome (2400 Euros), while Lottery A has only a 33% chance of the higher maximum (2500 Euros). The individual’s justification centers on the risk of losing out on the 2400 Euros (i.e., the certainty of the lower maximum) in exchange for a small chance at a higher maximum. The individual explicitly rejects the risk associated with the extra 100 Euros, which aligns with avoiding the lower probability of the higher outcome. This shows that the individual prioritized the certainty of the maximum outcome (2400 Euros) over the uncertain chance of a higher one (2500 Euros), which corresponds exactly to the decision reason: preferring the lottery with the higher probability of the maximum outcome. Therefore, the individual used the decision reason. The justification matches the rule of the reason both in content (focusing on the probability of the maximum outcome) and in logic (choosing certainty over a lower-probability higher payoff).",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

